EasyBMP installation and build instructions
===========================================

Requirements
------------

The Make build requires GNU Make, GCC with its C++ compiler support, and GNU
binutils (for `ar`). The CMake build requires CMake 3.14 or newer and a C++
compiler. The sample program uses GNU Make and G++.

Building the library
--------------------

From the repository root, run:

    make

This builds the static library at `build/EasyBMP.a`. To remove the build
outputs, run `make clean`.

Installing the library
----------------------

By default, `make install` installs the library, headers, and an EasyBMP
pkg-config file under `/usr/local`. Use an install prefix you can write to,
or run with the permissions needed for the chosen prefix:

    make PREFIX="$HOME/.local" install

The library is installed to `PREFIX/lib`, headers to `PREFIX/include/EasyBMP`,
and the pkg-config file to `PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig`. To uninstall from the
same prefix, run:

    make PREFIX="$HOME/.local" uninstall

When using a custom prefix, add `PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig` to `PKG_CONFIG_PATH`
if you want pkg-config to find EasyBMP.

Building and installing with CMake
----------------------------------

From the repository root, configure and build the library with:

    cmake -S . -B build-cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local"
    cmake --build build-cmake

Install the library, headers, CMake package files, and pkg-config file with:

    cmake --install build-cmake

The install directories are printed during configuration. To uninstall the
files listed in CMake's install manifest, run:

    cmake --build build-cmake --target uninstall

The CMake package can be used with `find_package(EasyBMP CONFIG REQUIRED)` and
the `EasyBMP::EasyBMP` target. When using a custom prefix, add its
`lib/pkgconfig` directory to `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` to find the pkg-config file.

Building the sample
-------------------

The sample program and its Makefile are in `sample/`. Build it from the
repository root with:

    make -C sample

This creates `sample/EasyBMPtest`. Run it from that directory:

    cd sample
    ./EasyBMPtest

The sample writes output BMP images in the sample directory. Remove the
sample build and generated output files with `make -C sample clean`.

Building the documentation
--------------------------

The user manual sources and Makefile are in `docs/`. Building the manual
requires LaTeX (`latex`) and `dvipdfm`. From the repository root, run:

    make -C docs

This builds `docs/EasyBMP_UserManual.pdf` and its DVI intermediate. See
`docs/EasyBMP_UserManual.tex` for the manual source.

Visual Studio
-------------

The repository also includes the Visual Studio solution
`EasyBMP.sln` and project files under `vstudio/` for building with Visual
Studio.
